WEBVTT

00:00:20.023 --> 00:00:21.454
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:21.772 --> 00:00:22.658
Sammy!

00:00:23.454 --> 00:00:25.635
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can! Go!

00:00:29.632 --> 00:00:30.655
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:32.722
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:36.817 --> 00:00:37.817
This is dad's book.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.617
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:41.775
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:41.844 --> 00:00:42.957
Family business.

00:00:43.116 --> 00:00:44.502
Do you think Mom wanted all this for us?

00:00:44.593 --> 00:00:45.706
I can't do this alone.

00:00:46.521 --> 00:00:47.520
I'm driving.

00:01:34.766 --> 00:01:36.379
Can't keep kids out of this place.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:37.765
What is it anyway?

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:39.287
I forgot you're not a local.

00:01:39.446 --> 00:01:40.469
You don't know the legend.

00:01:40.878 --> 00:01:41.650
Legend?

00:01:41.832 --> 00:01:43.768
Every town's got its stories, right?

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.836
Ours is Roosevelt asylum.

00:01:46.518 --> 00:01:48.790
They say it's haunted with
the ghosts of the patients.

00:01:49.227 --> 00:01:50.113
Spend the night,

00:01:50.613 --> 00:01:52.340
Spirits will drive you insane.

00:01:58.859 --> 00:01:59.791
Hello?!

00:02:00.222 --> 00:02:01.313
Police officers!

00:02:04.448 --> 00:02:05.812
Police officers!

00:02:14.366 --> 00:02:16.974
You tell me these kids
brought bolt cutters?

00:02:18.092 --> 00:02:18.865
Come on.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.024
Let's split up.

00:02:20.592 --> 00:02:21.523
All right.

00:02:35.724 --> 00:02:36.565
Hello?

00:03:05.516 --> 00:03:06.356
Hello?

00:03:29.964 --> 00:03:30.918
All right.

00:03:31.827 --> 00:03:33.076
Come on out.

00:04:01.491 --> 00:04:02.627
Kelly, you copy?

00:04:04.694 --> 00:04:05.558
Jeez!

00:04:06.376 --> 00:04:07.443
Where the hell you been?!

00:04:07.602 --> 00:04:08.398
In there.

00:04:08.511 --> 00:04:09.647
What was it? See anything?

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:13.677
No.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:22.639
This is patrol 1 4. We are
clear, we return to the station

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:43.351
Hey.

00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:52.540
So, what?

00:04:53.381 --> 00:04:54.812
You're still not talking to me?

00:04:58.018 --> 00:04:58.814
Walt.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.927
I said I was sorry about before.

00:05:00.972 --> 00:05:02.722
How many times do I have to say it?

00:05:23.402 --> 00:05:25.856
No, dad was in California
last we heard from him.

00:05:26.424 --> 00:05:29.128
We just thought if he
comes to you for munitions,

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.019
Maybe you've seen him
in the last few weeks.

00:05:31.299 --> 00:05:33.046
Just call us if you hear anything. Okay.

00:05:33.195 --> 00:05:34.093
Thanks.

00:05:35.053 --> 00:05:36.151
Caleb hasn't heard from him?

00:05:36.201 --> 00:05:36.874
Nope.

00:05:36.999 --> 00:05:39.244
Neither has Jefferson or pastor Jim.

00:05:39.668 --> 00:05:41.215
What about the journal?
Any leads in there?

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.887
No. Same last time I looked.

00:05:42.936 --> 00:05:44.458
Nothing I can make out.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.170
I love the guy, but I swear
he writes like freaking Yoda.

00:05:48.171 --> 00:05:49.667
And maybe we should call the feds,

00:05:49.817 --> 00:05:50.865
File a missing person's out.

00:05:50.866 --> 00:05:53.260
We talked about this. Dad would be
pissed if we put the feds on his tail.

00:05:53.261 --> 00:05:54.407
I don't care anymore

00:05:54.532 --> 00:05:56.550
After all that happened back in kansas,

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:57.573
I mean...

00:05:57.823 --> 00:05:58.771
He should have been there, Dean.

00:05:58.772 --> 00:06:00.791
You said so yourself. You
tried to call him and nothing.

00:06:00.866 --> 00:06:01.864
I know.

00:06:02.311 --> 00:06:03.658
I loose my cellphone.

00:06:03.758 --> 00:06:05.604
You know, he could be
dead for all we know.

00:06:05.605 --> 00:06:06.876
Don't say that.

00:06:07.201 --> 00:06:08.723
He's not dead. He's...

00:06:08.822 --> 00:06:11.118
He's what? He's hiding? He's busy?

00:06:17.579 --> 00:06:18.776
I don't believe it.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.323
What?

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:26.016
It's a-A text message.

00:06:27.213 --> 00:06:28.336
It's coordinates.

00:06:30.381 --> 00:06:32.253
You think dad was texting us?

00:06:32.449 --> 00:06:33.747
He's given us coordinates before.

00:06:33.797 --> 00:06:35.867
The man can barely work a toaster, Dean.

00:06:36.092 --> 00:06:37.439
Sam, this is good news.

00:06:37.539 --> 00:06:38.936
It means he's okay, or alive.

00:06:39.136 --> 00:06:40.757
Was there a number on the caller I.D.?

00:06:40.807 --> 00:06:42.005
Huh, it said "unknown."

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:43.332
Okay, well, where do
the coordinates point?

00:06:43.382 --> 00:06:44.655
That's the interesting part.

00:06:44.854 --> 00:06:46.301
Rockford, Illinois.

00:06:47.271 --> 00:06:48.469
Okay, and that's interesting how?

00:06:48.519 --> 00:06:51.313
I checked the local rockford
paper. Take a look at this.

00:06:54.678 --> 00:06:56.275
This cop, Walter Kelly,

00:06:56.499 --> 00:06:58.371
Comes home from his
shift, shoots his wife,

00:06:58.495 --> 00:07:00.541
Then puts the gun in his
mouth, blows his brains out.

00:07:00.641 --> 00:07:02.736
Earlier that night,
kelly and his partner

00:07:02.737 --> 00:07:05.294
Responded to a call at
the Roosevelt asylum.

00:07:05.369 --> 00:07:07.888
Okay, I'm not following. What
does this have to do with us?

00:07:07.889 --> 00:07:10.832
Dad earmarked the same
asylum in the journal.

00:07:11.603 --> 00:07:12.851
Let's see.

00:07:14.472 --> 00:07:15.171
Here.

00:07:15.246 --> 00:07:17.890
"Seven unconfirmed
sightings, two deaths"

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:19.487
Till last week, at least.

00:07:19.761 --> 00:07:21.556
I think this is where he wants us to go.

00:07:25.307 --> 00:07:26.429
This is a job.

00:07:28.275 --> 00:07:29.473
Dad wants us to work a job.

00:07:29.548 --> 00:07:31.244
Maybe we'll meet up with
him. Maybe he's there.

00:07:31.245 --> 00:07:32.317
Maybe he's not.

00:07:32.489 --> 00:07:34.560
May He could be sending us there
by ourselves to hunting thing.

00:07:34.561 --> 00:07:35.872
Who cares?

00:07:36.581 --> 00:07:38.477
If he wants us there,
it's good enough for me.

00:07:38.801 --> 00:07:40.523
This doesn't strike you as weird...

00:07:41.521 --> 00:07:42.494
The texting,

00:07:42.741 --> 00:07:44.013
The coordinates? Sam.

00:07:44.388 --> 00:07:46.533
Dad's telling us to go
somewhere. We're going.

00:08:07.517 --> 00:08:09.513
You're Daniel Gunderson,
right, you're cop?

00:08:09.688 --> 00:08:10.461
Yeah.

00:08:11.484 --> 00:08:12.332
I'm...

00:08:12.405 --> 00:08:13.677
Nigel Tufnel

00:08:13.727 --> 00:08:14.849
With the chicago tribune.

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:16.396
Do you mind if I ask a couple questions

00:08:16.397 --> 00:08:17.444
About your partner?

00:08:17.445 --> 00:08:18.392
Yeah, I do.

00:08:18.393 --> 00:08:19.365
I'm just trying to have a beer here.

00:08:19.366 --> 00:08:21.685
I just want to hear
the story in your words.

00:08:22.293 --> 00:08:24.363
A week ago, my partner
was sitting in that chair,

00:08:24.762 --> 00:08:25.910
And now he's dead.

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:27.157
Are you gonna ambush me here?

00:08:27.158 --> 00:08:27.931
Sorry,

00:08:27.932 --> 00:08:29.527
But I need to know what happened.

00:08:29.652 --> 00:08:32.421
Heyn buddy! How about leaving
the poor guy alone, huh?!

00:08:32.755 --> 00:08:35.200
The man's an officer! Why don't
you show a little respect?!

00:08:42.408 --> 00:08:43.531
You didn't have to do that.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:44.903
Yeah, of course I did.

00:08:45.635 --> 00:08:46.932
That guy's a serious jerk.

00:08:47.157 --> 00:08:49.028
Let me buy you a beer, huh?

00:08:49.701 --> 00:08:50.699
Two?

00:08:54.317 --> 00:08:55.090
Thanks.

00:09:00.156 --> 00:09:01.603
You shoved me kind of
hard in there, buddy boy.

00:09:01.628 --> 00:09:03.125
I had to sell it, didn't I?

00:09:03.774 --> 00:09:04.971
It's method acting.

00:09:06.019 --> 00:09:06.842
Huh?

00:09:07.339 --> 00:09:08.112
Never mind.

00:09:08.113 --> 00:09:09.235
What did you find out from Gunderson?

00:09:09.335 --> 00:09:11.006
So, Walter Kelly was a good cop.

00:09:11.231 --> 00:09:12.827
Head of his class, even-Keeled.

00:09:12.877 --> 00:09:14.224
He had a bright future ahead of him.

00:09:14.225 --> 00:09:14.873
What about at home?

00:09:14.874 --> 00:09:16.842
He and his wife had a few
fights. Like everybody.

00:09:16.892 --> 00:09:18.364
But it was mostly smooth sailing.

00:09:18.514 --> 00:09:20.110
They were even talking
about having kids.

00:09:20.111 --> 00:09:22.854
All right, so how the kelly had some
deep see the crazy way in the bus

00:09:22.855 --> 00:09:24.227
Or something else did it to him. Right.

00:09:24.324 --> 00:09:26.070
What did Gunderson tell
you about the asylum?

00:09:27.193 --> 00:09:27.891
A lot.

00:09:52.913 --> 00:09:55.632
So, apparently, the cops
chased the kids here...

00:09:57.451 --> 00:09:58.973
Into the south wing.

00:10:01.044 --> 00:10:02.216
South wing, huh?

00:10:02.834 --> 00:10:04.356
Wait a second.

00:10:05.579 --> 00:10:07.475
South wing, south wing.

00:10:10.493 --> 00:10:12.015
"1972,

00:10:12.215 --> 00:10:14.076
Three kids broke into the south wing.

00:10:14.201 --> 00:10:15.673
Only one survived."

00:10:15.872 --> 00:10:17.167
The way he tells it, one of his friends

00:10:17.168 --> 00:10:19.138
Went nuts and started
lighting up the place.

00:10:20.061 --> 00:10:21.707
So, whatever's going on,

00:10:21.882 --> 00:10:23.354
South wing seems like the heart of it.

00:10:23.404 --> 00:10:24.976
Yeah, but if kids are
spelunking the asylum,

00:10:24.977 --> 00:10:26.793
Why aren't there a ton more deaths?

00:10:28.789 --> 00:10:30.710
It looks like the doors
are usually chained.

00:10:31.758 --> 00:10:33.430
They could have been
chained up for years.

00:10:33.923 --> 00:10:35.670
Yeah, to keep people out.

00:10:36.318 --> 00:10:37.965
Or to keep something in.

00:10:48.319 --> 00:10:50.664
Let me know if you see any
dead people, Haley Joel.

00:10:50.814 --> 00:10:51.936
Dude, enough.

00:10:52.834 --> 00:10:54.553
I'm serious. You've got
to be careful. Right.

00:10:54.554 --> 00:10:56.748
Ghosts are attracted to
that E.S.P. Thing you got.

00:10:56.749 --> 00:10:57.946
I told you, it's not E.S.P.

00:10:57.947 --> 00:11:00.166
I just have strange vibes, sometimes,

00:11:00.765 --> 00:11:01.439
Weird dreams.

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:03.352
Yeah, whatever. Don't ask, don't tell.

00:11:03.577 --> 00:11:04.974
Do you get any reading
on that thing or not?

00:11:05.049 --> 00:11:06.970
No. Of course, it doesn't
mean nobody's home.

00:11:07.045 --> 00:11:09.290
Spirits can't appear
during certain hours of day.

00:11:09.315 --> 00:11:10.785
The freaks come out at night.

00:11:11.009 --> 00:11:11.982
Ya. Hey Sam

00:11:12.032 --> 00:11:13.554
Who do you think is a hotter psychic

00:11:13.629 --> 00:11:15.675
Patricia Arquette,
Jennifer Love Hewitt or you?

00:11:42.648 --> 00:11:43.621
Man.

00:11:44.869 --> 00:11:46.216
Electroshock,

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:49.032
Lobotomies. They did some
twisted stuff to these people,

00:11:49.257 --> 00:11:52.175
Kind of like my man
Jack in "cuckoo's nest."

00:11:56.063 --> 00:11:57.884
So, what do you think?

00:11:58.533 --> 00:12:00.154
Ghosts are possessing people?

00:12:00.803 --> 00:12:01.676
Maybe.

00:12:02.524 --> 00:12:05.518
Maybe it's more like Amityville
or the smurl haunting.

00:12:05.714 --> 00:12:08.010
Ah, spirits driving them insane,

00:12:08.633 --> 00:12:10.779
Kind of like my man
Jack in "the shining."

00:12:14.521 --> 00:12:15.491
Dean...

00:12:17.462 --> 00:12:18.585
When are we going to talk about it?

00:12:18.685 --> 00:12:19.333
Talk about what?

00:12:19.358 --> 00:12:20.955
About the fact that dad's not here.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.076
Oh, uh, let's see, never.

00:12:23.077 --> 00:12:24.024
I'm being serious, man.

00:12:24.025 --> 00:12:24.851
So am I, sam.

00:12:24.852 --> 00:12:27.321
Look. He sent us here. He
obviously wants us here.

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:28.643
We'll just have to pick
up the search later.

00:12:28.644 --> 00:12:30.215
It doesn't matter what he wants.

00:12:30.216 --> 00:12:32.556
See, that attitude right there,

00:12:33.055 --> 00:12:34.577
That is why I always
got the extra cookie.

00:12:34.701 --> 00:12:35.799
Dad could be in trouble.

00:12:35.874 --> 00:12:37.396
We should be looking for him.

00:12:37.421 --> 00:12:40.240
We deserve some answers, Dean. I mean,
this is our family were talking about..

00:12:40.241 --> 00:12:41.659
I understand that, sam,

00:12:41.809 --> 00:12:42.831
But he's given us an order.

00:12:42.832 --> 00:12:44.528
So what ? We've got to
always follow dad's orders?

00:12:44.553 --> 00:12:45.875
Of course we do.

00:12:56.896 --> 00:12:58.643
Sanford Ellicott

00:12:59.865 --> 00:13:00.888
You know what we got to do?

00:13:01.013 --> 00:13:03.103
We've got to find out
more about the south wing,

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:05.177
See if something happened here.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:22.778
Sam Winchester?

00:13:23.826 --> 00:13:24.575
That's me.

00:13:24.649 --> 00:13:25.647
Come on in.

00:13:31.953 --> 00:13:34.351
Thanks again for see me last minute.

00:13:49.495 --> 00:13:50.593
Dr. Ellicott?

00:13:51.413 --> 00:13:52.611
Ellicott, that name.

00:13:52.885 --> 00:13:55.929
Wasn't there a dr. Sanford Ellicott?

00:13:56.328 --> 00:13:58.947
Yeah, he was a chief
psychiatrist somewhere.

00:13:58.948 --> 00:14:01.989
My father was chief of staff
at the old Roosevelt asylum.

00:14:02.114 --> 00:14:03.162
How did you know?

00:14:03.785 --> 00:14:06.829
Huh, well, I'm sort of
a local-History buff.

00:14:06.976 --> 00:14:10.768
Hey, wasn't there an incident
or something in the...

00:14:10.968 --> 00:14:12.864
In the hospital, I guess,
in the south wing, right?

00:14:12.913 --> 00:14:14.435
We're on your dollar, Sam.

00:14:15.251 --> 00:14:16.873
We're here to talk about you.

00:14:17.796 --> 00:14:19.867
Oh, okay, yeah, yeah, sure.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:22.733
So? So.

00:14:22.858 --> 00:14:24.005
How's things?

00:14:24.205 --> 00:14:26.550
Uh, things are good, doctor.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:27.448
Good.

00:14:27.648 --> 00:14:28.895
What you been doing?

00:14:29.741 --> 00:14:30.863
Uh...

00:14:31.487 --> 00:14:33.632
Same old. I've just been on a...

00:14:33.707 --> 00:14:35.728
On a road trip with my brother.

00:14:35.803 --> 00:14:37.025
Was that fun?

00:14:39.094 --> 00:14:40.116
Loads.

00:14:40.665 --> 00:14:41.763
Um...

00:14:42.137 --> 00:14:43.310
You know... We...

00:14:44.507 --> 00:14:45.954
Met a lot of...

00:14:46.703 --> 00:14:47.825
Interesting people.

00:14:47.875 --> 00:14:48.624
Mm-Hmm.

00:14:48.775 --> 00:14:50.297
Did a lot of, uh...

00:14:51.394 --> 00:14:52.991
A lot of interesting things.

00:14:53.814 --> 00:14:54.937
Uh...

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:56.958
You know,

00:14:57.332 --> 00:14:58.430
What was it...

00:14:58.494 --> 00:15:00.415
Exactly that happened in the south wing?

00:15:00.465 --> 00:15:01.413
I forget... Look,

00:15:01.563 --> 00:15:02.960
If you're a local-History buff,

00:15:03.007 --> 00:15:05.003
Then you know all about
the Roosevelt riot.

00:15:05.353 --> 00:15:06.101
The riot?

00:15:06.126 --> 00:15:08.346
Well, no, I know, I'm
just curious -- Sam.

00:15:09.095 --> 00:15:10.517
Let's cut the bull, shall we?

00:15:11.263 --> 00:15:12.760
You're avoiding the subject.

00:15:15.953 --> 00:15:16.852
What subject?

00:15:16.951 --> 00:15:17.800
You.

00:15:18.423 --> 00:15:20.020
Now, I'll make you a deal.

00:15:20.691 --> 00:15:22.886
I'll tell you all
about the Roosevelt riot

00:15:23.061 --> 00:15:25.456
If you tell me something
honest about yourself...

00:15:26.129 --> 00:15:27.152
Like, uh...

00:15:27.748 --> 00:15:29.744
This brother you're road-Tripping with.

00:15:30.243 --> 00:15:31.715
How do you feel about him?

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:43.974
Dude.

00:15:44.074 --> 00:15:46.219
You were in there forever. What
the hell were you talking about?

00:15:46.566 --> 00:15:47.764
Just the hospital, you know.

00:15:47.838 --> 00:15:48.562
And?

00:15:48.637 --> 00:15:50.308
And the south wing,

00:15:50.408 --> 00:15:51.930
It's where they housed
the real hard cases,

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.776
Psychotics, the criminally insane.

00:15:53.823 --> 00:15:54.572
Sounds cozy.

00:15:54.597 --> 00:15:56.842
Yeah, and one night in '64, they rioted,

00:15:57.041 --> 00:15:58.962
Attacked the staff, attacked each other.

00:15:59.037 --> 00:16:00.609
So, what, the patients
took over the asylum?

00:16:00.756 --> 00:16:02.278
Apparently. Any deaths?

00:16:02.578 --> 00:16:04.524
Some patients, some staff.

00:16:04.648 --> 00:16:05.796
I guess it was pretty gory.

00:16:05.797 --> 00:16:07.542
Some of the bodies were
never even recovered,

00:16:07.642 --> 00:16:09.663
Including our chief of staff, Ellicott.

00:16:09.664 --> 00:16:10.935
What do you mean "Never recovered"?

00:16:10.963 --> 00:16:12.286
Cops scoured every inch of the place,

00:16:12.336 --> 00:16:14.207
But I guess the patients must have...

00:16:15.354 --> 00:16:17.625
Stuffed the bodies somewhere hidden.

00:16:17.996 --> 00:16:19.094
That's grim. Ya.

00:16:19.568 --> 00:16:21.738
So they transferred all
the surviving patients

00:16:21.739 --> 00:16:23.285
And shut down the hospital for good.

00:16:23.286 --> 00:16:26.275
All right so the * we've got a bunch of
violent deaths and unrecovered bodies.

00:16:26.276 --> 00:16:27.821
Which could mean a
bunch of angry spirits.

00:16:28.096 --> 00:16:30.404
Not good times. Let's check
out the hospital tonight.

00:16:51.127 --> 00:16:52.574
Check this out.

00:16:53.796 --> 00:16:54.769
Creepy...

00:16:56.571 --> 00:16:57.868
Yet terrifying.

00:16:59.739 --> 00:17:01.361
I thought we were going to a movie.

00:17:02.009 --> 00:17:03.881
This is better. It's
like we're in a movie.

00:17:05.774 --> 00:17:07.545
I can't believe you call this a date.

00:17:10.436 --> 00:17:11.858
Come on. That'll be fine.

00:17:12.407 --> 00:17:13.729
That's look around.

00:17:14.328 --> 00:17:15.500
Come on!

00:17:22.461 --> 00:17:23.484
What was that? Ugh!

00:17:27.077 --> 00:17:28.075
Hey, look.

00:17:28.297 --> 00:17:29.719
Come on, let's check it out.

00:17:30.093 --> 00:17:31.540
I don't want to.

00:17:32.314 --> 00:17:33.037
Let's just go.

00:17:33.087 --> 00:17:34.359
Come on.

00:17:37.136 --> 00:17:38.059
Okay.

00:17:38.433 --> 00:17:39.656
Okay. You can wait here.

00:17:39.756 --> 00:17:41.003
Gavin, no.

00:17:41.103 --> 00:17:42.325
I'm just gonna be a minute.

00:17:43.772 --> 00:17:45.693
Nothing's gonna get you, I promise.

00:18:38.496 --> 00:18:39.469
Damn it.

00:18:43.541 --> 00:18:45.761
Hey, sweetie, couldn't take it, huh?

00:18:50.125 --> 00:18:50.998
Hey.

00:18:55.813 --> 00:18:58.033
Gavin, where are you?

00:19:00.411 --> 00:19:01.434
Gavin.

00:19:30.518 --> 00:19:31.641
Getting readings?

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:33.137
No, big-Time.

00:19:33.362 --> 00:19:35.358
This place is orbing like crazy.

00:19:39.347 --> 00:19:41.393
There's probably multiple
spirits out and about.

00:19:41.439 --> 00:19:43.884
And if these unrecovered
bodies are causing the haunting?

00:19:43.885 --> 00:19:45.205
We got to find them and burn them.

00:19:45.255 --> 00:19:45.986
Just be careful.

00:19:45.987 --> 00:19:48.959
The only thing that makes me more
nervous than a pissed-Off spirit

00:19:49.446 --> 00:19:52.217
Is a pissed-Off spirit
of a psycho killer.

00:21:03.166 --> 00:21:03.901
Dean!

00:21:04.636 --> 00:21:05.258
Dean!

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:06.870
Shotgun!

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:08.341
Sam, get down!

00:21:18.425 --> 00:21:19.415
That was weird.

00:21:19.613 --> 00:21:20.320
Yeah,

00:21:20.715 --> 00:21:21.592
You're telling me.

00:21:23.571 --> 00:21:26.286
No, Dean, I mean, it was weird
that she didn't attack me.

00:21:26.377 --> 00:21:28.186
It looked pretty aggro
from where I was standing.

00:21:28.187 --> 00:21:29.431
She didn't hurt me.

00:21:29.515 --> 00:21:30.703
She didn't even try.

00:21:31.105 --> 00:21:33.452
So she didn't want to hurt
me, then what did she want?

00:22:02.512 --> 00:22:03.983
It's all right.We're
not going to hurt you.

00:22:05.821 --> 00:22:06.895
It's okay.

00:22:07.778 --> 00:22:08.457
What's your name?

00:22:08.485 --> 00:22:09.277
Katherine.

00:22:10.578 --> 00:22:11.454
Kat.

00:22:11.624 --> 00:22:12.359
Okay.

00:22:12.614 --> 00:22:13.660
I'm dean.This is sam.

00:22:13.661 --> 00:22:14.904
What are you doing here?

00:22:16.215 --> 00:22:18.025
My boyfriend, Gavin...

00:22:18.308 --> 00:22:19.354
Is he here?

00:22:19.954 --> 00:22:21.057
Somewhere.

00:22:21.735 --> 00:22:24.676
He thought it would be fun,
try and see some ghosts.

00:22:25.468 --> 00:22:27.193
I thought it was all just...

00:22:28.075 --> 00:22:29.065
You know...

00:22:29.800 --> 00:22:30.931
Pretend.

00:22:33.900 --> 00:22:35.003
I've seen things.

00:22:36.537 --> 00:22:38.431
I heard Gavin scream, and...

00:22:38.516 --> 00:22:40.184
All right, Kat, come on.

00:22:40.524 --> 00:22:42.446
Sam's gonna get you out of here.
Then we're gonna find your boyfriend.

00:22:42.464 --> 00:22:44.076
No, no.

00:22:45.179 --> 00:22:47.130
I'm not gonna leave without Gavin.

00:22:47.385 --> 00:22:48.685
I'm coming with you.

00:22:48.686 --> 00:22:50.728
It's no a joke around
here, okay. It's dangerous.

00:22:50.813 --> 00:22:52.509
That's why I've got to find him.

00:22:54.149 --> 00:22:55.846
All right, I guess we're
gonna split up, then.

00:22:56.096 --> 00:22:57.029
Let's go.

00:23:01.327 --> 00:23:02.401
Gavin!

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:06.990
Gavin!

00:23:10.157 --> 00:23:11.118
Gavin!

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:14.738
Gavin!

00:23:15.112 --> 00:23:16.497
I've got a question for you.

00:23:16.893 --> 00:23:18.816
You've seen a lot of
horror movies, yeah?

00:23:19.042 --> 00:23:19.834
I guess so.

00:23:19.835 --> 00:23:21.700
Do me a favor. Next time you see one,

00:23:21.870 --> 00:23:22.916
Pay attention.

00:23:23.351 --> 00:23:24.963
When someone says a place is haunted,

00:23:25.246 --> 00:23:26.349
Don't go in.

00:23:41.112 --> 00:23:41.875
Gavin?

00:23:42.497 --> 00:23:43.600
Hey, gavin.

00:23:44.477 --> 00:23:46.626
Hey, it's okay. It's
okay. I'm here to help.

00:23:47.333 --> 00:23:48.039
Who are you?

00:23:48.040 --> 00:23:49.375
My name is Sam.

00:23:49.884 --> 00:23:51.213
We found your girlfriend.

00:23:51.694 --> 00:23:52.571
Kat? Yeah.

00:23:52.572 --> 00:23:53.730
Is she all right?

00:23:53.934 --> 00:23:56.151
She's worried about you. Are you okay?

00:23:57.821 --> 00:23:59.484
I was running. I, uh,

00:23:59.614 --> 00:24:00.690
I think I fell.

00:24:00.691 --> 00:24:02.060
You were running from what?

00:24:03.854 --> 00:24:05.060
There was...

00:24:05.582 --> 00:24:08.328
There was this girl. Her-Her face...

00:24:09.925 --> 00:24:11.067
It was all messed up.

00:24:11.068 --> 00:24:12.110
Okay, listen, listen,

00:24:12.111 --> 00:24:14.099
This girl, did she try to hurt you?

00:24:14.726 --> 00:24:16.780
What? No, she, uh...

00:24:17.595 --> 00:24:18.867
She what?

00:24:20.041 --> 00:24:21.215
She kissed me.

00:24:23.700 --> 00:24:26.537
Um, but she didn't hurt you physically?

00:24:26.732 --> 00:24:28.656
Dude, she kissed me.

00:24:29.308 --> 00:24:30.482
I'm scarred for life.

00:24:31.760 --> 00:24:33.358
Trust me, it could have been worse.

00:24:33.359 --> 00:24:35.021
And now, do you remember anything else?

00:24:35.445 --> 00:24:36.619
She, uh...

00:24:37.467 --> 00:24:39.423
Actually, she tried to
whisper something in my ear.

00:24:40.050 --> 00:24:40.930
What?

00:24:41.745 --> 00:24:43.278
I don't know. I ran like hell.

00:24:57.991 --> 00:24:59.915
You son of a bitch.

00:25:00.697 --> 00:25:02.556
It's all right. I've got a lighter.

00:25:05.674 --> 00:25:07.663
Ow. You're hurting my arm.

00:25:08.674 --> 00:25:09.881
What are you talking about?

00:25:18.681 --> 00:25:21.355
Let me out!Please!

00:25:26.270 --> 00:25:28.433
Kat, hang on!

00:25:56.039 --> 00:25:56.985
What's going on?

00:25:56.986 --> 00:25:58.142
She's inside with one of them.

00:25:58.143 --> 00:25:59.382
Help me!

00:25:59.447 --> 00:26:00.197
Kat!

00:26:00.198 --> 00:26:01.469
Get me out of here!

00:26:01.470 --> 00:26:03.381
Kat, it's not gonna hurt you.

00:26:03.903 --> 00:26:06.544
Listen to me. You have to
face it. You have to calm down.

00:26:06.545 --> 00:26:07.693
She's got to what?

00:26:07.694 --> 00:26:08.606
I have to what?

00:26:08.607 --> 00:26:11.443
These spirits, they don't try to
hurt, they're trying to communicate.

00:26:11.444 --> 00:26:13.041
You've got to listen to.
You've got to face it.

00:26:13.042 --> 00:26:13.986
You face it.

00:26:13.987 --> 00:26:15.617
No. It's the only way you're
gonna get out of there.

00:26:15.618 --> 00:26:16.398
No!

00:26:16.399 --> 00:26:17.572
Look at it.That's all.

00:26:17.637 --> 00:26:18.974
Come on.You can do it.

00:26:40.522 --> 00:26:41.272
Kat?

00:26:43.164 --> 00:26:44.794
Now, I hope you're right about this.

00:26:46.791 --> 00:26:47.998
Yeah, me, too.

00:26:57.924 --> 00:26:59.065
Oh, Kat.

00:27:04.289 --> 00:27:05.659
1, 3, 7.

00:27:06.409 --> 00:27:07.452
Sorry?

00:27:08.789 --> 00:27:10.420
It whispered in my ear

00:27:10.811 --> 00:27:11.952
1, 3, 7.

00:27:12.937 --> 00:27:14.404
Room number.

00:27:17.698 --> 00:27:20.259
All right. So if these spirits
aren't trying to hurt anyone.

00:27:20.260 --> 00:27:21.825
Then what are they trying to do?

00:27:22.151 --> 00:27:23.423
Maybe that's what they've
been trying to tell us.

00:27:23.424 --> 00:27:24.564
I guess we'll find out.

00:27:25.249 --> 00:27:26.194
All right.

00:27:28.842 --> 00:27:29.723
So,

00:27:29.724 --> 00:27:31.940
Now, you guys ready to leave this place?

00:27:32.462 --> 00:27:33.669
That's an understatement.

00:27:33.702 --> 00:27:34.712
Okay.

00:27:35.136 --> 00:27:36.539
You get them out of here.

00:27:36.740 --> 00:27:38.469
I'm gonna gofind room 137.

00:27:47.438 --> 00:27:50.307
So, how do you guys know
about all this ghost stuff?

00:27:51.547 --> 00:27:53.405
It's kind of our job.

00:27:54.455 --> 00:27:56.412
Why would anyone want a job like that?

00:27:58.825 --> 00:28:00.944
I had a crappy guidance counselor.

00:28:03.201 --> 00:28:05.418
And Dean? He's your boss?

00:28:07.733 --> 00:28:08.614
No.

00:28:52.730 --> 00:28:53.740
All right.

00:28:54.001 --> 00:28:55.632
I think we have a small problem.

00:28:56.217 --> 00:28:57.260
Let's break it down.

00:28:57.423 --> 00:28:58.434
I don't think that's gonna work.

00:28:58.564 --> 00:28:59.445
Then a window.

00:28:59.446 --> 00:29:00.097
They're barred.

00:29:00.098 --> 00:29:01.793
How are we supposed to get out?

00:29:03.782 --> 00:29:05.510
That's the point. We're not.

00:29:06.071 --> 00:29:07.376
There's something in here.

00:29:07.506 --> 00:29:08.712
It doesn't want us to leave.

00:29:11.060 --> 00:29:11.941
Those patients.

00:29:12.006 --> 00:29:12.952
No.

00:29:13.473 --> 00:29:14.582
Something else.

00:29:40.340 --> 00:29:42.851
This is why I get paid the big bucks.

00:29:49.400 --> 00:29:50.737
"Patients journal."

00:30:06.934 --> 00:30:09.542
All work and no play makes Dr. Ellicott,

00:30:09.680 --> 00:30:11.669
A very dull boy.

00:30:19.601 --> 00:30:21.390
Right. I've looked everywhere.

00:30:21.672 --> 00:30:22.767
There's no other way out.

00:30:23.143 --> 00:30:24.128
So, what the hell are we gonna do?

00:30:24.191 --> 00:30:25.745
For starters, we're not gonna panic.

00:30:25.885 --> 00:30:26.949
Why the hell not?

00:30:29.484 --> 00:30:30.110
Hey.

00:30:30.157 --> 00:30:31.189
Sam, it's me.

00:30:31.659 --> 00:30:33.364
I see it. It's coming at me.

00:30:33.682 --> 00:30:34.401
Where are you?

00:30:34.402 --> 00:30:35.481
I'm in the basement. Hurry up!

00:30:35.512 --> 00:30:36.420
I'm on my way.

00:30:36.670 --> 00:30:38.751
All right. Can either
of you handle a shotgun?

00:30:39.158 --> 00:30:40.112
What?! No!

00:30:40.566 --> 00:30:41.270
I can.

00:30:42.980 --> 00:30:44.763
My dad took me skeet
shooting a couple times.

00:30:44.810 --> 00:30:45.655
Oh, I heard.

00:30:45.796 --> 00:30:46.828
It's loaded with rock salt.

00:30:46.875 --> 00:30:47.845
Now, it might not kill a spirit,

00:30:47.892 --> 00:30:49.394
But it will repel it,
so if you see something,

00:30:49.551 --> 00:30:50.051
Shoot.

00:30:50.067 --> 00:30:50.724
Okay.

00:30:50.959 --> 00:30:51.569
Okay.

00:30:58.286 --> 00:30:59.083
Dean!

00:31:17.655 --> 00:31:18.515
Dean!

00:32:19.622 --> 00:32:20.452
Dean?

00:32:48.013 --> 00:32:49.296
Don't be afraid.

00:32:49.640 --> 00:32:51.142
I'm going to make you all better.

00:32:58.447 --> 00:32:59.495
Hey, Gavin.

00:33:01.237 --> 00:33:01.941
Yeah?

00:33:03.677 --> 00:33:05.398
If we make it out of here alive,

00:33:06.587 --> 00:33:08.105
We are so breaking up.

00:33:11.544 --> 00:33:12.592
Did you hear that?

00:33:12.764 --> 00:33:13.828
Something's coming.

00:33:17.489 --> 00:33:18.882
Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

00:33:19.492 --> 00:33:20.822
Don't shoot! It's me!

00:33:21.072 --> 00:33:22.735
Sorry. Sorry.

00:33:23.314 --> 00:33:24.581
Son of a...

00:33:28.915 --> 00:33:30.167
What are you still doing here?

00:33:30.438 --> 00:33:31.392
Where's Sam?

00:33:31.705 --> 00:33:33.144
He went to the basement. You called him.

00:33:33.989 --> 00:33:34.787
I didn't call him.

00:33:34.917 --> 00:33:36.043
His cellphone rang.

00:33:36.340 --> 00:33:37.295
He said it was you.

00:33:39.329 --> 00:33:40.314
Basement, huh?

00:33:44.630 --> 00:33:45.474
All right.

00:33:46.585 --> 00:33:47.571
Watch yourselves.

00:33:49.761 --> 00:33:50.856
And watch out for me.

00:33:57.080 --> 00:33:57.878
Sammy?

00:33:59.615 --> 00:34:00.866
Sam, you down here?

00:34:01.758 --> 00:34:02.572
Sam!

00:34:05.075 --> 00:34:05.971
Sam!

00:34:08.303 --> 00:34:09.038
Man...

00:34:09.820 --> 00:34:11.432
Answer me when I'm calling you.

00:34:11.995 --> 00:34:12.574
You all right?

00:34:12.575 --> 00:34:13.638
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:34:13.779 --> 00:34:15.202
You know that wasn't
me who called, right?

00:34:15.300 --> 00:34:17.286
Yeah, I know. I think
something lured me down here.

00:34:17.287 --> 00:34:18.648
I think I know who

00:34:18.867 --> 00:34:19.727
Dr. Ellicott.

00:34:20.169 --> 00:34:22.375
That's what the spirits have been trying
to tell us. You haven't seen him, have you?

00:34:22.469 --> 00:34:23.283
No.

00:34:23.471 --> 00:34:24.425
How do you knowit was him?

00:34:24.426 --> 00:34:25.770
Because I found his logbook.

00:34:25.802 --> 00:34:28.336
Apparently, he was
experimenting on his patients.

00:34:28.826 --> 00:34:29.952
Awful stuff.

00:34:29.983 --> 00:34:31.658
Makes lobotomies look
like a couple of aspirin.

00:34:31.659 --> 00:34:33.300
But it was the patients who rioted.

00:34:33.301 --> 00:34:35.053
Yeah. They were rioting
against Dr. Ellicott.

00:34:36.304 --> 00:34:39.782
Dr. Feelgood was working on some
sort of extreme-Rage therapy.

00:34:39.783 --> 00:34:42.113
He thought if he could get his
patients to vent their anger,

00:34:42.223 --> 00:34:43.506
Then they'd be cured of it.

00:34:43.897 --> 00:34:45.196
Instead it only made
them worse and worse

00:34:45.197 --> 00:34:46.447
And angrier and angrier.

00:34:46.651 --> 00:34:48.090
I'm thinking, what if his spirit

00:34:48.309 --> 00:34:49.529
Is doing the same thing?

00:34:49.764 --> 00:34:50.531
To the cop,

00:34:50.645 --> 00:34:52.022
The kids in the '70s

00:34:52.335 --> 00:34:54.697
Making them so angry
they become homicidal.

00:34:55.777 --> 00:34:56.449
Come on.

00:34:56.731 --> 00:34:58.421
We've got to find his
bones and torch them.

00:34:58.921 --> 00:34:59.766
How?

00:35:00.086 --> 00:35:01.400
The police never found his body.

00:35:01.462 --> 00:35:04.185
The logbook said he had some
hidden procedure room down here

00:35:04.186 --> 00:35:06.328
Somewhere where he'd
work on his patients. So,

00:35:06.474 --> 00:35:08.273
If I was a patient, I'd
drag his ass down here

00:35:08.274 --> 00:35:09.634
Do a little work on myself.

00:35:09.681 --> 00:35:11.089
I don't know.It sounds kind of...

00:35:11.152 --> 00:35:11.871
Of crazy?

00:35:11.872 --> 00:35:12.387
Yeah.

00:35:12.388 --> 00:35:13.858
Yeah, exactly.

00:35:29.858 --> 00:35:31.110
I told you I looked everywhere.

00:35:31.111 --> 00:35:32.815
I didn't find a hidden room.

00:35:33.191 --> 00:35:34.771
Well, that's why they call it hidden.

00:35:37.701 --> 00:35:38.765
You hear that?

00:35:40.204 --> 00:35:41.112
What?

00:35:51.978 --> 00:35:53.229
There's a door here.

00:35:56.609 --> 00:35:57.532
Dean.

00:36:02.938 --> 00:36:04.518
Step back from the door.

00:36:09.472 --> 00:36:10.818
Sam, put the gun down.

00:36:11.193 --> 00:36:12.351
Is that an order?

00:36:14.025 --> 00:36:15.699
That's more of a friendly request.

00:36:15.700 --> 00:36:17.999
'Cause I'm getting pretty
tired of taking your orders.

00:36:19.631 --> 00:36:20.726
I knew it.

00:36:21.321 --> 00:36:22.479
Ellicott did something
to you, didn't he?

00:36:22.480 --> 00:36:23.699
For once in your life,

00:36:24.122 --> 00:36:25.029
Shut your mouth.

00:36:25.030 --> 00:36:26.427
What are you gonna do, sam?

00:36:26.953 --> 00:36:28.696
The gun's filled with rock salt.

00:36:28.888 --> 00:36:29.920
It's not gonna kill me.

00:36:33.284 --> 00:36:33.910
No.

00:36:34.207 --> 00:36:35.115
But it'll hurt like hell.

00:36:43.108 --> 00:36:43.906
Sam.

00:36:44.531 --> 00:36:46.112
We've got to burn Ellicott's bones,

00:36:46.143 --> 00:36:47.520
And all this will be over,

00:36:47.885 --> 00:36:49.105
And you'll be back to normal.

00:36:49.277 --> 00:36:50.325
I am normal.

00:36:51.358 --> 00:36:52.969
I'm just telling the
truth for the first time.

00:36:53.470 --> 00:36:55.191
I mean, why are we even here?

00:36:55.989 --> 00:36:58.685
'Cause you're following dad's
orders like a good little soldier?

00:36:58.779 --> 00:37:01.297
'Cause you always do what
he says without question?

00:37:01.595 --> 00:37:03.597
Are you that desperate for his approval?

00:37:03.801 --> 00:37:05.240
This isn't you talking, Sam.

00:37:05.308 --> 00:37:06.904
That's the difference
between you and me.

00:37:07.123 --> 00:37:09.000
I have a mind of my own.

00:37:09.250 --> 00:37:11.018
I'm not pathetic like you.

00:37:11.019 --> 00:37:13.099
So what are you gonna do?
Huh. You gonna kill me?

00:37:13.146 --> 00:37:16.072
We're no closer to finding dad today

00:37:13.146 --> 00:37:16.072
You know, I am sick of
doing what you tell me to do.

00:37:16.562 --> 00:37:18.456
We're no closer to finding dad today

00:37:18.564 --> 00:37:20.395
Than we were six months ago.

00:37:22.277 --> 00:37:23.560
Well, then here.

00:37:23.810 --> 00:37:25.641
Let me make it easier for you.

00:37:27.831 --> 00:37:28.801
Come on.

00:37:28.989 --> 00:37:29.943
Take it.

00:37:30.297 --> 00:37:33.144
Real bullets are gonna work a hell
of a lot better than rock salt.

00:37:34.208 --> 00:37:35.100
Take it.

00:37:46.981 --> 00:37:48.483
You hate me that much?

00:37:50.110 --> 00:37:51.941
You think you can kill your own brother?

00:37:54.819 --> 00:37:56.164
Then go ahead.

00:37:57.385 --> 00:37:58.652
Pull the trigger.

00:38:05.011 --> 00:38:06.231
Do it!

00:38:23.773 --> 00:38:26.120
Man, I'm not gonna give
you a loaded pistol.

00:38:33.597 --> 00:38:34.833
Sorry, Sammy.

00:39:38.269 --> 00:39:39.739
Oh, that's just gross.

00:39:48.804 --> 00:39:49.884
Soak it up.

00:40:02.761 --> 00:40:04.170
Don't be afraid.

00:40:05.003 --> 00:40:06.396
I'm going to help you.

00:40:06.505 --> 00:40:08.336
I'm going to make you all better.

00:40:59.524 --> 00:41:01.386
You're not gonna try
and kill me, are you?

00:41:04.296 --> 00:41:05.125
No.

00:41:05.959 --> 00:41:06.815
Good.

00:41:08.196 --> 00:41:10.152
'Cause that would be awkward.

00:41:16.350 --> 00:41:17.492
Thanks, guys.

00:41:17.821 --> 00:41:19.010
Yeah, thanks.

00:41:19.401 --> 00:41:21.466
No more haunted asylums, okay?

00:41:28.894 --> 00:41:29.864
Hey, Dean.

00:41:31.256 --> 00:41:32.837
I' sorry, man. I

00:41:34.088 --> 00:41:35.950
said some awful thingsback there.

00:41:36.518 --> 00:41:37.785
You remember all that?

00:41:38.176 --> 00:41:39.037
Yeah.

00:41:40.727 --> 00:41:43.605
It's like I couldn't control
it, but I didn't mean it

00:41:44.012 --> 00:41:44.982
Any of it.

00:41:45.671 --> 00:41:46.625
You didn't, huh?

00:41:47.647 --> 00:41:48.664
No. Of course, not.

00:41:51.532 --> 00:41:53.112
Do we need to talk about this?

00:41:54.129 --> 00:41:55.005
No.

00:41:55.091 --> 00:41:57.868
I'm not really in the sharing
and caring kind of mood.

00:41:58.474 --> 00:42:00.023
I just want to get some sleep.

00:42:15.337 --> 00:42:16.197
Dean.

00:42:23.835 --> 00:42:24.695
Hello.

00:42:27.699 --> 00:42:28.419
Dad?



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
